From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GUIWindowSettingsCategory: do not take a film's output mode for the GUI resolution

With a settings category on screen, every window resize that leaves the
graphic context's video resolution different from the GUI's current one is
taken as a change of the GUI resolution: it is saved to
videoscreen.screenmode, and CDisplaySettings asks "Keep this resolution?"
from that setting's change callback, still inside CSettingsManager::SetString,
which holds the settings lock shared. A film started while the window is shown
(from a remote, JSON-RPC, a playlist or an add-on) switches the output to its
own mode, so the film's refresh rate is saved as the GUI's and the dialog
opens. Its render loop processes the player's switch to fullscreen video,
and closing the settings window unregisters its setting callbacks, which takes
that lock exclusively on the thread already holding it shared (CSharedSection
is not reentrant): Kodi's main thread blocks for good, video freezes with
audio still playing and JSON-RPC stops answering. Seen on an Amlogic box with System > Display open when a
3D film started; any refresh-rate switch reaches it.

While a video is playing the output follows the film, not the GUI setting,
so the resize is no longer taken as a resolution change then; when playback
ends the output returns to the GUI mode and the check finds nothing to save.

The same lock is held across the prompt when the resolution is changed by
hand, so a film started while that prompt is up still deadlocks; closing that
would mean not holding the settings lock across a setting's callbacks, in
shared settings code, and is left alone here.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/settings/windows/GUIWindowSettingsCategory.cpp b/xbmc/settings/windows/GUIWindowSettingsCategory.cpp
index 657ad77..f9ff071 100644
--- a/xbmc/settings/windows/GUIWindowSettingsCategory.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/settings/windows/GUIWindowSettingsCategory.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
 #include "GUIPassword.h"
 #include "GUIUserMessages.h"
 #include "ServiceBroker.h"
+#include "application/ApplicationComponents.h"
+#include "application/ApplicationPlayer.h"
 #include "input/actions/Action.h"
 #include "input/actions/ActionIDs.h"
 #include "settings/DisplaySettings.h"
@@ -107,7 +109,12 @@ bool CGUIWindowSettingsCategory::OnMessage(CGUIMessage &message)
     {
       if (message.GetParam1() == GUI_MSG_WINDOW_RESIZE)
       {
-        if (IsActive() && CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetCurrentResolution() != CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetVideoResolution())
+        // while a video plays the output follows the film, not the GUI setting
+        const auto& components = CServiceBroker::GetAppComponents();
+        const auto appPlayer = components.GetComponent<CApplicationPlayer>();
+        if (IsActive() && !(appPlayer && appPlayer->IsPlayingVideo()) &&
+            CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetCurrentResolution() !=
+                CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetVideoResolution())
         {
           CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().SetCurrentResolution(CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetVideoResolution(), true);
           CreateSettings();
